The `format` value is validated against a fixed allowlist (`supported_explain_formats`) in the base `explain_query_prefix` before the MySQL/PostgreSQL overrides append it, so it is allowlisted. However, the PostgreSQL override interpolates the **option names** (`name.upper()`) directly into the SQL text via `'%s %s' % i`, and the base method only raises for options when `validates_explain_options` is True — which PostgreSQL sets to `False`. Since `explain(**options)` is a public API, an attacker-controlled option name is concatenated into the executed SQL without any allowlist.

